<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  File associations for the native formats and the App Paths key. The
  embedded plugins — archives, associations for their formats and selection
  page — are in the neighboring fragment plugins.generated.wxs (gitignored),
  which the xtask generates on every build from the bundling strategy
  (bundled-plugins.txt, otherwise bundled-plugins.default.txt; cf.
  xtask/src/bundled.rs). Both fragments are wired in by
  tauri.msi.conf.json.

  ── Why the plugins do not go through bundle.resources ───────────────────────
  `bundle.resources` works, but Tauri generates **one component per file** for
  it, with random identifiers on every build
  (`<Component Id="I0373392f…">`). Yet WiX forbids adding a condition to a
  component declared elsewhere: a plugin cannot be made uncheckable as long as
  it comes from there. The `<File>`s are therefore declared in the generated
  fragment, one component conditioned per plugin. The archives all stay in the
  MSI's cab — only the checked ones are written to disk.

  The source path goes through `$(sys.SOURCEFILEDIR)` (candle intrinsic
  variable = the .wxs's folder) and not through a path relative to the current
  directory: Tauri does not expose the cwd it launches candle/light with.
  `bundled::stage` (xtask) fills `src-tauri/bundled-plugins/` before
  bundling and fails if an archive is missing.

  Nothing to do on the Rust side: `plugins::seed_bundled` installs at first
  launch whatever it finds in `resource_dir()/bundled-plugins/`, hence
  exactly the checked plugins. Unchecking a plugin **already installed** does
  not uninstall it: the seeding only adds and updates, it never removes (a
  plugin placed by hand must not disappear).

  ── Why the associations do not go through bundle.fileAssociations ───────────
  Same reason, taken one step further: the bundler generates them in the
  executable's component, where they would necessarily follow the application
  — hence unconditional. Yet those of the formats served by a plugin must
  follow **the plugin**, not the application. Hence the complete rewrite as
  registry writes, and `bundle.fileAssociations` deliberately absent from
  tauri.msi.conf.json.

  ── Two association levels ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Windows distinguishes two writes:

    Software\Classes\<.ext>\(Default) = ProgID   claims the DEFAULT handler
    Software\Classes\<.ext>\OpenWithProgids      adds to "Open with" (« Ouvrir avec »)

  Claiming the default only works on a **virgin** extension: as soon as a
  `UserChoice` exists (HKCU, hash-protected since Windows 8), the
  `(Default)` is ignored and the application only appears as a suggestion. It
  OVERWRITES, however, the `(Default)` value in place, which MSI does not
  restore on uninstall.

  - `.kdws .kdext` and the extensions of the installed plugins — `(Default)` +
    `OpenWithProgids`: this is what makes the double-click work, the
    installer's whole purpose. A plugin's formats are claimed without
    distinction, shared ones included (`.tex`, `.csv`): installing a plugin is
    an explicit choice, and the `UserChoice` of anyone who already picked
    another application wins anyway;
  - the shared native formats (`.md`, `.txt`, `.html`…) — `OpenWithProgids`
    **alone**. Kroki Desk is offered in "Open with" (« Ouvrir avec »), the
    application in place is not touched (`.html` → `htmlfile`, `.txt` →
    `txtfilelegacy`), and uninstalling leaves nothing behind.

  ── What stays conditioned: the extensions served by a plugin ────────────────
  An extension only makes sense if the plugin that reads it is there. Its
  components (one per plugin, ProgID `KrokiDesk.<Plugin>` included) therefore
  carry the plugin's condition, and only they do: the native formats below
  install unconditionally.

  ── The dialog (generated fragment) ──────────────────────────────────────────
  Tauri uses WixUI_InstallDir (Welcome → InstallDir → VerifyReady), which has
  no customization page. `PluginDlg` slips in between InstallDir and
  VerifyReady by overriding the `NewDialog` ControlEvents: for this event the
  Publish with the highest `Order` whose condition is true wins, hence
  Order="5" (WixUI_InstallDir goes up to 4) and the reuse of its path
  validation condition. The Tauri template plays the same trick at
  Order="2" to skip the license page. With no embedded plugin, the page is not
  generated.

  An unchecked box empties its `PLUGIN_<ID>` property: the component's
  condition becomes false, neither the archive nor its associations are
  installed. The properties are `Secure="yes"` — without that, the UI, which
  runs under the user's account, would not pass them to the elevated execution
  server, and everything would be installed whatever is unchecked. They are
  public, hence settable in a silent installation:
  `msiexec /i kroki_deskapp.msi /qn PLUGIN_CSV_TABLES=1 PLUGIN_LATEX_DOC=""`.

  ── App Paths: launching the application by name ─────────────────────────────
  The MSI does not add the application to the PATH (one more folder for every
  command of every terminal, for a single exe). The
  `App Paths\kroki_deskapp.exe` key is enough for `start kroki_deskapp …` (cmd),
  `Start-Process kroki_deskapp …` (PowerShell) and Win+R: these are the
  ShellExecute routes, and precisely the ones an agent or a script should
  take (`kroki_deskapp "modele.tex#eq:x"`): launched directly from bash while
  the application was closed, the exe would only hand control back when it
  exits. CreateProcess and bash's command resolution do not read this key, and
  need not. Unconditional: it follows the executable, not a plugin.

  Wired in by `wix.fragmentPaths` + `wix.componentGroupRefs`: **all** the
  ComponentGroups (this one and the two of the generated fragment) must be
  referenced, otherwise their components are attached to no feature.
  The executable is designated by `[INSTALLDIR]kroki_deskapp.exe` and not by the
  file reference `[#Path]`: Tauri injects the componentGroupRefs into its
  `External` feature while the exe belongs to `MainProgram`, and MSI refuses
  cross-feature file references (ICE69, a link error). The binary's name comes
  from the crate (`BIN_NAME` in xtask/src/main.rs): renaming it requires
  editing it here.
-->
<Wix xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/wix/2006/wi">
  <Fragment>

    <DirectoryRef Id="TARGETDIR">

      <!-- The ProgIDs themselves, shared by several components. A ProgID
           with no associated extension is inert. -->
      <Component Id="AssocProgIds" Guid="11F8BC6C-85C4-45AD-987F-89BE6DF7E36F">
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Kroki Desk\FileAssociations"
                       Name="progids" Type="integer" Value="1" KeyPath="yes" />

        <RegistryKey Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\KrokiDesk.Session" ForceDeleteOnUninstall="yes">
          <RegistryValue Type="string" Value="!(loc.KdProgIdSession)" />
          <RegistryValue Key="DefaultIcon" Type="string" Value="[INSTALLDIR]kroki_deskapp.exe,0" />
          <RegistryValue Key="shell\open\command" Type="string"
                         Value="&quot;[INSTALLDIR]kroki_deskapp.exe&quot; &quot;%1&quot;" />
        </RegistryKey>

        <RegistryKey Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\KrokiDesk.Plugin" ForceDeleteOnUninstall="yes">
          <RegistryValue Type="string" Value="!(loc.KdProgIdPlugin)" />
          <RegistryValue Key="DefaultIcon" Type="string" Value="[INSTALLDIR]kroki_deskapp.exe,0" />
          <RegistryValue Key="shell\open\command" Type="string"
                         Value="&quot;[INSTALLDIR]kroki_deskapp.exe&quot; &quot;%1&quot;" />
        </RegistryKey>

        <RegistryKey Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\KrokiDesk.Document" ForceDeleteOnUninstall="yes">
          <RegistryValue Type="string" Value="!(loc.KdProgIdDocument)" />
          <RegistryValue Key="DefaultIcon" Type="string" Value="[INSTALLDIR]kroki_deskapp.exe,0" />
          <RegistryValue Key="shell\open\command" Type="string"
                         Value="&quot;[INSTALLDIR]kroki_deskapp.exe&quot; &quot;%1&quot;" />
        </RegistryKey>
      </Component>

      <!-- Launch by name (`start kroki_deskapp`), cf. header. -->
      <Component Id="AppPath" Guid="5814141A-DECD-4E39-80B9-3316872CB2E2">
        <RegistryKey Root="HKMU" ForceDeleteOnUninstall="yes"
                     Key="Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\App Paths\kroki_deskapp.exe">
          <RegistryValue Type="string" Value="[INSTALLDIR]kroki_deskapp.exe" KeyPath="yes" />
          <RegistryValue Name="Path" Type="string" Value="[INSTALLDIR]" />
        </RegistryKey>
      </Component>

      <!-- The application's own formats: the `(Default)` really takes hold,
           and it is what makes the double-click work. Nothing to overwrite —
           these extensions belong to no one else. The plugins' extensions
           follow the same regime, in the generated fragment. -->
      <Component Id="AssocOwnFormats" Guid="875EDF93-7B0C-4D84-9112-1BF9ADBBB599">
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Kroki Desk\FileAssociations"
                       Name="own" Type="integer" Value="1" KeyPath="yes" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\.kdws" Type="string" Value="KrokiDesk.Session" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\.kdws\OpenWithProgids"
                       Name="KrokiDesk.Session" Type="string" Value="" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\.kdext" Type="string" Value="KrokiDesk.Plugin" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\.kdext\OpenWithProgids"
                       Name="KrokiDesk.Plugin" Type="string" Value="" />
      </Component>

      <!-- Shared formats, native to the application: "Open with" (« Ouvrir avec ») alone.
           The <.ext> key often pre-exists and belongs to someone else —
           no ForceDeleteOnUninstall, no `(Default)` value set. -->
      <Component Id="AssocSharedFormats" Guid="271F5138-DB48-4AAD-87F7-0208A7EA8CCA">
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Kroki Desk\FileAssociations"
                       Name="shared" Type="integer" Value="1" KeyPath="yes" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\.md\OpenWithProgids"
                       Name="KrokiDesk.Document" Type="string" Value="" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\.markdown\OpenWithProgids"
                       Name="KrokiDesk.Document" Type="string" Value="" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\.mdown\OpenWithProgids"
                       Name="KrokiDesk.Document" Type="string" Value="" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\.mkd\OpenWithProgids"
                       Name="KrokiDesk.Document" Type="string" Value="" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\.txt\OpenWithProgids"
                       Name="KrokiDesk.Document" Type="string" Value="" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\.html\OpenWithProgids"
                       Name="KrokiDesk.Document" Type="string" Value="" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Classes\.htm\OpenWithProgids"
                       Name="KrokiDesk.Document" Type="string" Value="" />
      </Component>

    </DirectoryRef>

    <ComponentGroup Id="KrokiDeskAssociations">
      <ComponentRef Id="AppPath" />
      <ComponentRef Id="AssocProgIds" />
      <ComponentRef Id="AssocOwnFormats" />
      <ComponentRef Id="AssocSharedFormats" />
    </ComponentGroup>

  </Fragment>
</Wix>
